// ---- node bank address per (layer, slot) ---------------------------
// A slot serves one node per LAYER (that is what makes the lattice shared),
// so a per-slot table cannot carry the address: it needs the layer too.
// The RTL knows the layer it runs (SLICEBASE[slice] + SLOTLAY[slot]) and
// reads this table as [(layer*NSLOT + slot)*AW +: AW].
// The spatial index is slot mod P -- folding the slot's own layer in
// aliases slot 0 of two layers, a bug this build hit.
